
  First, what I found in the repo:

  index.html   (11 lines — <h1>Tasks</h1> and an empty <main>)
  1 commit: "initial: empty tasks page"

  That's the whole app. No tasks, no data model, no users, no server, no JS, no package manifest, no tests.

  [1mScope flag before we go further.[0m The request as stated — "users get notified when tasks they care about change" —
  presupposes four things that don't exist here yet:

  1. [1mTasks[0m — a data model, storage, and a way to create/edit them
  2. [1mUsers[0m — identity, so "users" and "they care about" mean something
  3. [1mChange events[0m — something that detects and records a task changing
  4. [1mNotification delivery[0m — the part you actually asked for

  Only #4 is notifications. The other three are prerequisites. I don't want to spend our questions refining delivery
  channels and digest schedules for a system that has no tasks to notify about — that's how you end up with a
  beautifully specced subsystem bolted to nothing.

  So my first question is the one that reframes everything else.
